Z||000000||fropuff||06-27-2001||11:45 PM||||Hey guys.  I've got a little problem with the idle on my 2.8L automatic 86 GT.  It's when it's in gear (drive or reverse).  When it's in park or neutral, the RPMs are at 1000-1100.  When it's in gear and stopped with my foot on the brake, the RPMs go down to around 600 and the car stumbles.  If I approach a stop fast enough, the car almost dies.  It even died once today on a hill.  I was wondering what I can do to fix it.  I don't really like having to put it in neutral and rev it up a little at the stop lights.  Can I alter the idle to go up to around 1000 when in gear?  Thanks for any help.    <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||06-28-2001||05:03 PM||||Did you check the timming?  Give it a tune-up?  Maybe a bad sensor?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||06-28-2001||06:25 PM||||How old are the plug wires, they do deteriorate.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||06-28-2001||06:37 PM||||Get off your @ss and get to work!<BR>OOOOH, sorry, couldn't resist the groaner...<P>Any codes stored??<BR>Last one I fixed with a similar complaint was the MAP...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Denny||06-28-2001||09:07 PM||||Common problem with the automatic -- it's the torque converter clutch solenoid not releasing.  Replace the solenoid.||||reg||12
Z||000005||fropuff||06-29-2001||12:19 AM||||Thanks for the replies.  It's not that I'm lazy; I just have no idea what to look for.  Why can't I ask, then get to work?  Anyway, the plug wires are a little over a year old w/ maybe 1500 miles on them.  I'll ask the mechanic tomorrow what he thinks it is.  I'm sure it's one that you guys said.  I'll check the timing.  If the torque convertor clutch soleniod is cheap enough, I'll get it.  I plan on doing a 3800 Series II swap this winter, and it's not that bad.  At least it didn't stall today.  It gets in the 600 RPM range, but then goes up a little.  I'll check it out and let you know.  Thanks again!||||reg||1
